sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant H as Host client
  participant GH as Gateway (host's)
  participant R as Room actor (owner node)
  participant RD as Redis snapshot
  participant BUS as NATS room topic
  participant GN as Gateways x ~50 (listener sockets)
  participant L as 5,000 listener clients

  H->>GH: pause {cmdId, baseVersion=n}
  GH->>R: command (auth + rate limit passed)
  Note over R: Serialised in the actor. Check host, epoch, version.<br/>pos = P0 + (now - T0). New state: playing=false, P0=pos, T0=now, version=n+1
  par fan-out first
    R->>BUS: publish state(n+1, epoch, serverTime)
  and persist in parallel
    R->>RD: write snapshot (write-behind, ~ms)
  end
  BUS->>GN: state(n+1) to every gateway that has members
  GN->>L: one ~200 byte frame per socket (about 100 per gateway)
  Note over L: audio.pause() immediately, show frozen position P0.<br/>No per-listener ack (would be 5,000 replies)
  GN-->>H: same state frame = confirmation (optimistic UI settles, or rolls back on reject)
  L-->>BUS: 1% sampled telemetry: applied_at - serverTime
  Note over H,L: Budget: host to gateway ~30 ms, actor + bus under 5 ms, gateway to listener 20-100 ms.<br/>p95 end-to-end about 150 ms. Resume is scheduled: play {startAt = now + 600 ms}, so everyone starts together.
